Update an existing IAM IP group.

Usage:
  confluent iam ip-group update <id> [flags]

Examples:
Update the name and CIDR blocks of IP group "ipg-12345":

  $ confluent iam ip-group update ipg-12345 --name "New Group Name" --cidr-blocks 123.234.0.0/16,168.150.200.0/24

Flags:
      --name string           Updated name of the IP group.
      --cidr-blocks strings   A comma-separated list of CIDR blocks in IP group.
      --context string        CLI context name.
  -o, --output string         Specify the output format as "human", "json", or "yaml". (default "human")

Global Flags:
  -h, --help            Show help for this command.
      --unsafe-trace    Equivalent to -vvvv, but also log HTTP requests and responses which might contain plaintext secrets.
  -v, --verbose count   Increase verbosity (-v for warn, -vv for info, -vvv for debug, -vvvv for trace).
